  "pattern": "recursion-termination",
  "difficulty_rating": 1675,
  "explanation": "Each leaf returns the shared ledger.balance — the cumulative running total — instead of that leaf's own cost, and the parent then re-sums these inflated values. The recursion terminates, but the root prints 45 instead of the real total 20.",
  "prompt": "This rolls up a cost from child units while a ledger accumulates. Step through and predict the total it prints.",
  "language": "javascript",
  "snippet": "function costRun(unit, ledger) {\n  ledger.balance += unit.cost;\n  if (unit.children.length === 0) {\n    return ledger.balance;\n  }\n  let subtotal = unit.cost;\n  for (const child of unit.children) subtotal += costRun(child, ledger);\n  return subtotal;\n}\nconst rootNode = {\n  cost: 10,\n  children: [{ cost: 5, children: [] }, { cost: 5, children: [] }],\n};\nconsole.log(costRun(rootNode, { balance: 0 }));",
